i.github.com/users/Zocker1999NET/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zocker1999NET/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zocker1999NET/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zocker1999NET/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zocker1999NET/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zocker1999NET/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zocker1999NET/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zocker1999NET/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zocker1999NET/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-13T10:06:35Z","updated_at":"2025-12-13T10:06:35Z","body":"> Generate a key using the command line:\n> ```\n> docker exec -it headscale \\\n>   headscale preauthkeys create --user myfirstuser --reusable --expiration 24h\n> ```\n\nI want to make aware that this has worked in earlier versions of headscale (at least in 0.25.1 because that is what its NixOS test at that time used, see [this line](https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/da2b89022cf3da1045c8cc9bb5c816de22fdd788/nixos/tests/headscale.nix#L81)).\nAnd actually I would be interested to know why this was changed 🤔 ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3649176933/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/4028933538","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/2631#issuecomment-4028933538","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2631","id":4028933538,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz887wJKWi","user":{"login":"tgrushka","id":89836285,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5ODM2Mjg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89836285?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgrushka","html_url":"https://github.com/tgrushka","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgrushka/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgrushka/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgrushka/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgrushka/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgrushka/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgrushka/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgrushka/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgrushka/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tgrushka/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-10T06:05:39Z","updated_at":"2026-03-10T06:05:39Z","body":"Huh, I just came across this again, maybe I can try contributing. Can't be that hard.... uh oh, don't jinx it! Probably not easy, else it would have been done? I guess would have to ensure lookup of user id everywhere, which would need to do db lookups, perhaps add a cache if one does not exist... uh oh.... But the foundation must be there, because the `acl.json` uses fully qualified usernames, and some of the commands do as well, so will have to take a dive into the code and see.\n\nTrying to get headscale up and running again and figure out `acl.json`, tagging, etc., I just thought to myself:\n\n**Q: What would Linux users worldwide say** if Linus Tarvolds suddenly changed the kernel to no longer accept alphanumeric usernames and required every `chown`, `su`, `setuid`, etc. command to use the numeric id instead?\n\n**A: They would riot.** There would be torches, pitchforks, and a thousand new angry GitHub issues per hour after all programs/scripts stopped working and systems no longer booted. Power would blackout worldwide. Linus would get an earful (if the internet 